ust we all made fast friends and  and yeah we still keep in touch this day  and talk every now and then  and we and darby's mom and dad were on  set who i get on with very well and that  helped it feel like a family and we kept  my head away from the set which would  have obviously not made it feel like a  family because he would have been grumpy  all the time and been a real sour  atmosphere so i made sure he wasn't  anywhere near the set and i really hoped  darby could you have ever imagined that  you'd be doing a car chase scene where  you were the one driving at your age  i never would have guessed i mean i mean  ever since i was younger i've always  wanted to do a car chase scene like i  just thought that was so cool and i  always been interested in like that  would be so cool just to like drive a  car just like go for go for it you know  like in a car chase oh that was so cool  so once i was finally a part of one i  felt so honored and grateful that i got  to i was like oh my gosh i'm gonna get  to drive the moving van let's go i get  set and i don't actually get to drive it  i get to sit in the driver's seat and  pretend like i'm driving and i was a  little bit disappointed  but it's okay because it was hooked up  to the trailer and then people would  walk by on the street and look in to the  van and be like is that a child in the  driver's seat of a moving truck and i'd  be like oh yeah don't worry it is but um  i'm not actually driving sadly but i  think i think for safety reasons it was  okay that i wasn't driving  but um i think that was all um also like  one of my favorite scenes  jack what was it like to get to shoot  the big fat scene in the deli and pretty  much pick up and throw anything you  could at bad guys  uh yeah i mean that was so much fun that  was a scene that we spent a lot of time  choreographing with the stance  department and it suddenly just in the  middle of the movie turns into a jackie  chan film it was great fun to to shoot  um and 